    {
      "id": "6470211a319f16af85640f03c953d2e4330fd6af",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1204413183,
          "type": null,
          "body": "@martin.r.mathieson there is not a bug about check length for FT_BOOLEAN ? -> packet-usb-ccid.c filter= usbccid.dwFeatures.autoIfsd  - mask has odd number of digits 0x400 expected max for FT_BOOLEAN is 8",
          "author": {
            "id": 279822,
            "username": "alagoutte",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Alexis La Goutte",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a15cba6417f4d1723eb56add7099bcfd8df373dc520577958b33c37915ef231b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/alagoutte"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-12-11T17:36:28.992Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-12-11T17:36:28.992Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 193686346,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 9072,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11b05f99cbf701763a89dfa9b2e486ac30338ef4",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1204415496,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I don't know whether its worth warning about anything here.  I saw some cases with odd number of digits - 3 may be easy to read, but when its 5 or more, it could be confusing to read/write.  When there are 7, I would question it should have been 6 or 8, etc.\n\nThe number of bits here is 32, which means the expected max number of digits would be 8. \nIf > 8 are given, that is surely an error.\n\nMaybe the ideal would be that if the field width is 32 bits, 8 digits are always given.  Then, for a 32-bit field, you could find the position of the bit(s) by reading from left or right. This may be too much to ask of dissector authors though.\n\nWhat do you think?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-12-11T17:52:28.430Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-12-11T17:52:28.430Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 193686346,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 9072,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8c6c7c0c106cfd3220eb87b77e7d0462b25d2f7b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1206147736,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Yes, it will be better for me, to set 32bits -> 8 digits (and get a warning /error if not the good length)",
          "author": {
            "id": 279822,
            "username": "alagoutte",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Alexis La Goutte",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a15cba6417f4d1723eb56add7099bcfd8df373dc520577958b33c37915ef231b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/alagoutte"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-12-12T19:47:13.085Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-12-12T19:47:13.085Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 193686346,
